From 8eca114df9110d649a3c5c6c344f02bee895f3da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:31:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/18] decmap: decode maps measured; three decoder-only
 speedups kept

Stored decode maps were measured and rejected: khuf decode tables in the
frame cost 4-8 KiB per block for at most 8% of decode; 8 -> 255 sampled
inverse-BWT indexes stay inside the noise at 1 and 4 threads; GR6+ field
searches are 8.5% of its decoder and CM tables are already built once per
process (0.3 ms). Kept, with no frame changing (determinism hashes equal):

- x86 AVX2 word-transform decoder (src/arch/x86_64/word_avx2.c, CPUID):
  text eco/hc decode +14.8% (1 thread) / +12.1% (4), JSON +13.7% / +12.1%
- khuf (codec 27): one 11-bit decode table instead of two, bit reversal
  from a constant table: khuf decode +7.6% to +8.9% on Silesia
- KLZH (codec 29): one validation pass, refills only when needed:
  decode +10% to +17%; KOLMO_NATIVE=all frames +16.3% / +14.2%

Benchmarks, tools and per-file results in benchmark/rc3w3/decmap; ledger
rows in research/CODECS.md. Bindings' native sources synced with src
(this also adds the native-lane files that were not yet synced).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4ZHnq84yP7cf4gzNv4
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

